    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>NOAA weather records can help connect hail or wind damage at your McAllen property to a specific storm date.</li>
<li>The NCEI Storm Events Database is the official long-term record; it is updated monthly and typically published after a delay of a few months.</li>
<li>NWS Local Storm Reports and Storm Prediction Center reports appear quickly but are preliminary.</li>
<li>A nearby report does not prove damage at your property, and a missing report does not prove there was none.</li>
<li>Weather data works best combined with a physical inspection, dated photos, and collateral damage evidence.</li>
